from pathlib import Path
import csv,random,sqlite3,json,io
p=Path(__file__).parent
r=random.Random(28)
rows=[]
for m in range(1,13):
 for category,price,cost in [('Furniture',25000,18000),('Technology',40000,26000),('Office Supplies',5000,2500)]:
  for region in ['East','West','Central']:
   for n in range(5):
    q=r.randint(1,8); discount=r.choice([0,10,20,30]); sales=q*price*(100-discount)//100; cogs=q*cost
    rows.append((len(rows)+1,f'2025-{m:02d}-15',category,region,q,discount,sales,cogs,sales-cogs))
cols=['line_id','date','category','region','quantity','discount_pct','sales_cents','cogs_cents','gross_profit_cents']
with (p/'sales.csv').open('w') as f:
 w=csv.writer(f);w.writerow(cols);w.writerows(rows)
sql='''-- SQLite; all monetary inputs are integer CAD cents.
SELECT COUNT(*) AS lines, SUM(sales_cents)/100.0 AS revenue,
 SUM(gross_profit_cents)/100.0 AS gross_profit,
 100.0*SUM(gross_profit_cents)/SUM(sales_cents) AS margin_pct FROM sales;
SELECT category, SUM(sales_cents)/100.0 AS revenue, SUM(gross_profit_cents)/100.0 AS gross_profit,
 100.0*SUM(gross_profit_cents)/SUM(sales_cents) AS margin_pct FROM sales GROUP BY category;
SELECT discount_pct, SUM(sales_cents)/100.0 AS revenue,
 100.0*SUM(gross_profit_cents)/SUM(sales_cents) AS margin_pct FROM sales GROUP BY discount_pct;
'''
(p/'analysis.sql').write_text(sql)
con=sqlite3.connect(':memory:');con.execute('CREATE TABLE sales ('+','.join(c+(' TEXT' if c in ['date','category','region'] else ' INTEGER') for c in cols)+')');con.executemany('INSERT INTO sales VALUES (?,?,?,?,?,?,?,?,?)',rows)
assert len(rows)==540 and len(set(x[0] for x in rows))==540
assert all(x[6]-x[7]==x[8] for x in rows)
queries=[x.strip() for x in sql.split(';') if x.strip()]
# Strip introductory SQL comment separately because its semicolon is punctuation.
queries=sql[sql.index('SELECT'):].split(';')
results=[con.execute(q).fetchall() for q in queries if q.strip()]
assert results[0][0][1]==sum(x[6] for x in rows)/100
(p/'results.json').write_text(json.dumps(results,indent=2))
a=results[0][0]; cats=results[1]; discs=results[2]
svg='<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" width="1000" height="620" viewBox="0 0 1000 620"><rect width="1000" height="620" fill="#101b2b"/><g fill="#eef4ff" font-family="Arial"><text x="40" y="50" font-size="28">Retail sales &amp; profitability</text><text x="40" y="80">Synthetic scenario | 2025 | CAD | 540 transaction lines</text>'
for i,(label,value) in enumerate([('Revenue',f'${a[1]:,.0f}'),('Gross profit',f'${a[2]:,.0f}'),('Gross margin',f'{a[3]:.1f}%')]):
 x=40+i*320;svg+=f'<text x="{x}" y="135" font-size="16">{label}</text><text x="{x}" y="175" font-size="32">{value}</text>'
svg+='<text x="40" y="240" font-size="22">Gross margin by category</text>'
for i,(cat,rev,gp,margin) in enumerate(cats):
 y=290+i*75;svg+=f'<text x="40" y="{y}">{cat}</text><rect x="210" y="{y-20}" width="{margin*13}" height="28" fill="#44d4b0"/><text x="{230+margin*13}" y="{y}">{margin:.1f}%</text>'
svg+='<text x="40" y="555">Gross profit excludes shipping, returns, tax and operating costs.</text><text x="40" y="585">Illustrative generated data; findings are not real retailer performance.</text></g></svg>'
(p/'dashboard.svg').write_text(svg)
(p/'README.md').write_text(f'''# Retail sales and profitability\n\nSynthetic retail case study · SQL · KPI design · Power BI implementation guide\n\n## Business brief\nA fictional retail manager needs to understand category profitability and discount exposure before setting promotion rules. Decisions: which categories deserve margin protection, and which discount bands require review?\n\n## Results\n- Revenue: CAD {a[1]:,.2f}; gross profit: CAD {a[2]:,.2f}; weighted gross margin: {a[3]:.2f}%.\n- Category margins: {', '.join(f'{c}: {m:.2f}%' for c,_,_,m in cats)}.\n- Discount-band margins: {', '.join(f'{d}% discount: {m:.2f}% margin' for d,_,m in discs)}.\n\n![Dashboard](dashboard.svg)\n\n## Recommendations and limits\nReview furniture promotions first because its modeled unit cost leaves less room for discounting. Require a projected gross-margin check before deep promotions. Test promotion changes against units sold and total gross profit; do not assume higher margin percentage maximizes profit. Discount relationships are mechanically generated from fixed category prices and costs, not causal evidence of consumer behavior. No real company, customer, or performance claims are made. Gross profit is not net profit.\n\n## Reproduce\nRequires Python 3 standard library only. Run `python3 build.py` from this folder. It deterministically regenerates sales.csv, analysis.sql, results.json, dashboard.svg and this README. No external packages or data downloads. The script creates an in-memory SQLite table and executes the SQL queries.\n\n## Data provenance and dictionary\nOriginal synthetic data generated by build.py, seed 28; 12 months × 3 categories × 3 regions × 5 lines = 540. No personal data or external dataset. Currency: CAD; no currency conversion. Each row is a transaction line, not necessarily a distinct customer or order.\n\n|Column|Meaning|\n|---|---|\n|line_id|Unique integer line key|\n|date|ISO date; monthly representative date, not actual daily activity|\n|category|Furniture, Technology, Office Supplies|\n|region|East, West, Central; fictional segments|\n|quantity|Units, integer 1–8|\n|discount_pct|Percent off list price: 0, 10, 20, 30|\n|sales_cents|Quantity × category price × (1 − discount/100)|\n|cogs_cents|Quantity × category unit cost|\n|gross_profit_cents|Sales less COGS|\n\n## Validation\nRun includes assertions for 540 unique line keys, row-level profit reconciliation and SQL revenue reconciliation to Python totals. Integer cents avoid currency rounding drift. Margin is SUM(profit)/SUM(sales), never an average of row margins. Results are saved in query order in results.json.\n\n## Power BI implementation\nNo PBIX is included or claimed. Import sales.csv with Get Data → Text/CSV. Set date to Date and monetary columns to Whole number. Create these measures and format as CAD or percent:\n\n```dax\nRevenue = DIVIDE(SUM(sales[sales_cents]), 100)\nGross Profit = DIVIDE(SUM(sales[gross_profit_cents]), 100)\nGross Margin = DIVIDE([Gross Profit], [Revenue])\n```\n\nAdd KPI cards, category margin bars, monthly revenue and gross profit lines, and region/category/discount slicers. Use a date table related one-to-many to sales[date] for time intelligence. Acceptance: unsliced cards match the totals above; selecting a category matches analysis.sql; zero revenue returns blank margin. dashboard.svg is a static verified analysis visual, not a Power BI report export.\n''')
(p/'linkedin-draft.md').write_text(f'''My first analytics portfolio case study: retail sales and profitability.\n\nUsing clearly labeled synthetic data, I built reproducible Python/SQLite analysis, defined weighted gross margin, and designed a dashboard with a Power BI implementation guide.\n\nThe scenario generated CAD {a[1]:,.2f} revenue at {a[3]:.2f}% gross margin. I explored how category cost structures and discount bands affect profit—and why margin percentage alone cannot determine a promotion strategy.\n\nThe repository includes data, SQL, validation checks, visuals and business recommendations. These are illustrative results, not real retailer performance.\n\nhttps://github.com/nayeemkhan28/analytics-portfolio/tree/main/01-retail-profitability\n\n#DataAnalytics #SQL #PowerBI #BusinessAnalysis\n''')
print(json.dumps({'metrics':a,'checks':'passed','files':[f.name for f in p.iterdir() if f.is_file()]}))
